# Declaring a subtype changes how the run's type tests are written, and that
# was enough to leave some of std/regexp's predicates read only for their
# tag. A release build's link let dead-argument elimination narrow those
# predicates' two-word return to one word while each still ended in a
# `musttail` call returning two, and the verifier aborted the link. Found by a
# generated program on 2026-09-28.
import "std/regexp"

type pt
  n

type tg pt

pub play = print "{regexp/find "a" "b"}"
